  "question": "What is the smallest copied composition contract that keeps kit membership, installation metadata and toolbar policy explicit?",
  "model": "GPT-6 (Codex)",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v3; redesign-from-first-principles; maximum-value hard cut; bounded owner and consumer census",
  "trigger": "The user challenged the duplicated onFinalFocus/focusEditorRef protocol in More, Mode and List controls, asked why registry transforms.ts survives, and asked whether slash.tsx boilerplate belongs in a package.",
  "requirements": [
    "Preserve provider-native focus restoration for Escape and outside close while allowing a selected edit action to return focus to the exact editor view.",
    "Keep menu lifecycle in copied provider adapters; Plate and Plite own editor behavior, not Radix/Base close sequencing.",
    "Preserve typed plugin insertion, matching-empty reuse, different-empty replacement, selection, atomic combobox completion and one-step undo.",
    "Keep labels, icons, grouping, product membership and asynchronous UI actions under copied presentation ownership.",
    "Delete a helper or protocol when its job can be routed through the existing canonical adapter, plugin portal or Plite structural primitive.",
    "Review the complete bounded focus-ref and insertion-helper owner set and record proof limits without implementing on audit authority."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Rechecked the stale ui decision against all six current focusEditorRef callers, both provider adapters, the two transforms.ts production consumers, typed plugin insertion, Plite block insertion and current transaction tests. Retained the prior rejection of a universal command catalog and the direct typed-operation direction. Reopened the adapter-completion and bounded-helper survival claims because current call sites expose repeated owner-level protocols.",
  "summary": "Pursue deleting six caller-owned mutable-ref close-focus handshakes through an item-scoped post-close focus contract in the copied provider adapter. Supersede survival of registry transforms.ts: Plite already owns structural empty replacement and Plate typed plugin operations own semantic targets, so the raw transaction matcher/callback recipe should disappear into the typed insertion path. Keep copied presentation and direct feature operations; do not add a Plate/Plite menu-focus API or universal command catalog. Two bounded units reviewed, zero excluded and zero unresolved.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-17-ui-source-and-command-ownership",
